
AWS Elastic IP Mapping Automation

This repository outlines the Terraform tasks executed by the Nautilus DevOps team to map and attach an existing Elastic IP resource to an active EC2 compute resource in the us-east-1 cloud zone.

📋 Task Parameters

• Working Directory: /home/bob/terraform
• Target File: main.tf
• EC2 Resource Handle: devops-ec2
• Elastic IP Allocation Tag: devops-ec2-eip
• Primary Deployment Cloud Zone: us-east-1

🛠️ Configuration Steps

The automation layout maps out infrastructure components sequentially while omitting duplicate declaration structures from existing root templates.
::: tabs

1. Unified Main Code configuration

Ensure the execution state includes tracking variables for the instance allocation matching the parameters block.
hcl
resource "aws_eip" "ec2_eip" {
  tags = {
    Name = "devops-ec2-eip"
  }
}

resource "aws_instance" "devops_ec2" {
  ami           = "ami-0c7217cdde317cfec"
  instance_type = "t2.micro"

  tags = {
    Name = "devops-ec2"
  }
}

resource "aws_eip_association" "eip_assoc" {
  instance_id   = aws_instance.devops_ec2.id
  allocation_id = aws_eip.ec2_eip.id
}


2. Execution Run Command

Execute the configuration directly from your integration window workspace to tie the allocated parameters together:
bash
terraform apply -auto-approve
Use code with caution.
:::

